# <claudes_code_comments>
# ** WHAT THIS FILE IS **
# The definition of branch triple-all-fastest since the round 8 ruling
# (2026-09-17-R8-RESULT-hitsfirst-alone-beats-through-the-noise-the-winners-tree-does-not.md
# section 5): THE NEW TIP PLUS THE HITSFIRST LEVER, hitsfirst ON by default, and nothing else.
# The navigator's standing rule is that the all-fastest default follows the measured number,
# and hitsfirst alone holds two sealed wins and no sealed loss:
#     round 4   +6.47 %   4/4   floor 2.71    (2026-09-17-R4-RESULT-*.md)
#     round 8   +12.31 %  4/4   floor 10.69   (2026-09-17-R8-RESULT-*.md)
# Provisional on round 9 (2026-09-17-R9-PREREGISTERED-RULE.txt), which re-measures hitsfirst,
# pool, winners, stack+hits and triple-all on a quiet box with the warm-up run. If round 9 ranks
# another tree above hitsfirst on a clean floor, the default moves again and this file with it.
#
# The line kinds are stack.manifest's (legend on tag sealed/all-fastest-tenlever-oldbase, the
# ten-lever tree this branch used to be); the machinery is the same build_stack.sh /
# stack_resolve.py / stack_list_conflicts.py, copied from triple-winners so the branch is
# self-contained.
#
# ** DEFAULTS **
# hitsfirst ON - the lever's own default (cuda_hits_first_enabled in ds4_cuda.cu:
# DS4_CUDA_HITS_FIRST=0 turns it off; DS4_CUDA_HITS_FIRST_STAGED=0 keeps hits-first with the
# single-stage read order). No default flip, no `local` line, no `patch` line: nothing in this
# tree is code that the lever does not carry.
#
# ** DERIVATION **
#   base        git rev-parse triple-tip-2026-09-16
#   lever sha   git rev-parse triple-hitsfirst~1   (the code commit under the round 4 card
#                                                    commit 40cd5b944, which is README-only)
#   resolve     none. triple-hitsfirst is a linear descendant of 12997e9c8 (505ac7f0d the card,
#               3e4773671 the code, 40cd5b944 the card again), so its diff against the base is
#               exactly its own code and applies with zero conflict hunks.
#   identity    git diff triple-hitsfirst -- '*.c' '*.h' '*.cu' '*.cuh' Makefile tests/  ->  EMPTY
#
# ** THE CHECK **
#   bash build_stack.sh allfastest.manifest --check <HEAD of triple-all-fastest>
#   Build surface byte-identical, 2026-09-17. The full tree differs by the documentation and
#   tooling files this branch carries (README.md, this manifest, the machinery), and the check
#   prints that difference rather than hiding it.
#   ⚠ NOT COMPILED FOR CUDA HERE. The Spark built this exact lever tree for round 8
#   (r8-hitsfirst @40cd5b94, ds4-server .text 24,886,127) and is running it in round 9.
# </claudes_code_comments>

base        12997e9c84b39258f28781b808d18ea0069af2ac
paths       *.c *.h *.cu *.cuh *.inc Makefile tests/ cuda/ speed-bench/*.c gguf-tools/
lever-base  12997e9c84b39258f28781b808d18ea0069af2ac

# --- the one lever ---------------------------------------------------------------------
lever   triple-hitsfirst                3e477367150ff20d1b5b93dd28b20b82452bf941   on
